WEBVTT

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.260
I can't--

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.300
I can't reach it.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.320
It stopped.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.570
Where are we?

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.740
I don't really know.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.040
EPISODE 3: LUNATIC SEVEN

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.830
I didn't know
that this tube was here either.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.660
We have air.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.330
This is probably a pathway
for maintenance drones.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.500
It connects to someplace with oxygen.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.720
What if we can't get out of here?

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.840
Nobody is dying today.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.510
Ouch!

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.560
How do you know that?

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.770
Because that's what's written
in the Seven Poem.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:03.850
PROPHECIES

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.850
Please leave out the occult.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.270
In situations like these, you just do
what you need to do based on science.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.480
I'll do what I need to do.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.610
Mina, everybody!

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.620
So we've escaped
to some kind of unknown tube.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.240
And who saved us?

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.120
Why, this stuffed animal did.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.330
Who are you?

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.500
I am Anshin-kun, the station fairy.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.050
Right.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.340
But who's inside?

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.510
There isn't anybody inside.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.180
-Who's that?
-It's the chief.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.890
Oh, the chief. I see now.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.180
I don't get it! Chief of what?

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.980
Come on now. Pop out, why don't you?

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.780
What? Just an old guy?

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.740
He's not just an old guy.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.250
He's the chief designer of this station--
Kokubunji.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.250
The ex-designer.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.800
When Deegle acquired it,
they kindly fired me.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.510
Then does that mean
you know all about this station?

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.140
-Do you know where we should run away to?
-Yeah.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:24.560
-Really?
-I designed it up to a point after all.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.980
But this is different
from what I remember.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.020
Did you say "up to a point"?

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.900
Up to what point?

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.480
About 70%.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.230
So you're not familiar with the other 30%?

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.410
There's oxygen
on the other side of this hatch.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.910
Push me.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.500
Everybody push.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.710
All right. We're safe.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.970
That's lucky.
The spare battery is still alive.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.470
But it probably won't last for long.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:07.430
This is a shop for tourists
to arrange an EVA.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.850
What is an EVA?

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.190
It's spacewalking.
You put on a space suit and go outside.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.270
Nasa, are you okay?

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.650
This is the Apollo space suit.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.740
-What's this?
-Don't touch that!

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.280
There is no air
on the other side of this bulkhead.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.990
There's a breach beyond this point.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.040
Open it and it's curtains for you.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.250
Then it's a dead end.
Where do we get on the shuttle?

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.960
It's the ring pathway.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.710
If we walk all the way to the Mars dome,
then we should be able to get to the top.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.590
-What?
-The ring pathway isn't connected.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:44.340
That's right.
It hasn't been constructed yet.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.300
The other side hasn't yet either.

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.010
Air is leaking out too.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.680
Soon, humans won't be able
to occupy this spot either.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.690
Will we die? Are we going to die?

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.230
We are not dying yet.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.190
The next cylinder over still has power.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.990
Our only option is to go there.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.490
But there's no pathway.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.240
There's a way.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.330
We're gonna go outside
and walk on the drone catwalk.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.290
Outside? As in out in space?

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.000
Obviously.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.800
Yes. We get to do an EVA.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.050
No way.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:24.220
Isn't that something
only people with training can do?

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.890
-Yeah.
-Yep.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.640
I can't do that.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.220
Don't worry.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.430
I have loads of EVA experience.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.810
You'll be fine if you follow me.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:39.400
Look, I'm even in my personalized
space suit already.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.240
This is an Orlan.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.950
-What's that?
-An antique space suit.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.450
Fine. Just close it!

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.620
I made it to meet demand for the mascot
off the station,

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:55.370
but I never got any offers.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.710
Now the time to use it has--

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.420
Chief?

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.340
Who the hell are you people?

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.010
Calm down, Chief.

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.220
Sit down over here.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.100
Not again.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.230
What was that?

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.190
Idiopathic dementia.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.690
It occasionally flares up.
He recovers right away though.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:22.440
Chief, could you tell me your name?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.690
I'm Anshin-kun.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.120
I'll go get the space suits.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:33.620
No way. I can't do it.
I've never spacewalked before.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.750
Find something
that is within our capabilities!

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.880
Then stay here and die.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.040
-What?
-Touya.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.840
Space is true nature.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.840
True nature is not your friend.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:47.930
SPACE IS OUR FRIEND!

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.720
It will kill humans caught off guard.
It's your enemy.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.470
What is that supposed to mean?

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.730
The people who have no will to live
will get left behind.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.560
I'm am so going to broadcast you
when this is over.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:04.820
I'm sorry. He doesn't mean it.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:08.490
But Touya is right.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:10.780
You can complain all you want,
but you'll only die.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.740
What? Are you taking his side?

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.950
That and I've wanted to try an EVA.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.000
I'm going to go help Touya.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.790
What? Stupid brother.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.210
I can't get on the shuttle
unless I can get to the dome.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.800
This has holes in it.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.800
This is also under maintenance.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:34.260
This is bad.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.850
There aren't any usable space suits.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:39.100
I'll help too.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.310
I've studied the equipment.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.770
-Yeah, help us out.
-Okay.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.980
By the way,

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:48.950
I really respect you, Touya.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:53.070
There will be more people like you
in the future,

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:55.830
and you will represent humanity.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.660
Also, Seven said the same thing.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.710
Humanity must leave Earth.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.090
Yes, I know.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.970
I'm sorry
for flicking your forehead before.

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:13.090
No way. I'm honored. Please do it again.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:15.300
I don't think so.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.100
Sup?

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:22.100
I plan on surviving too, so I'll help.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:28.280
-Konoha.
-Yes, Mina?

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.400
Sorry about before.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.990
I was out of line with that question.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:34.410
Don't worry about it.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:39.700
Okay. I'm going survive no matter what
and beat his follower count.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.290
-Touya.
-What?

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:47.750
I want you to lead us
when we do the EVA over there.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:48.750
What?

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:52.590
Nasa is injured, and I'm worried
about the chief's dementia.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.390
You do it.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:58.600
You're really like a leader.
You're arrogant and all.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:01.480
I don't have experience in space.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.600
Touya,
you're the most suited for this.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.940
We don't really need a leader, do we?

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.320
There's no up or down in space.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.530
Yes, we do need one.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:17.070
I'm just saying
I'm not very good at reading the room.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.280
We know.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:21.080
There are no rooms in space,
so you'll be fine.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.080
Don't blame me if we fail.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.000
Then it's settled.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.000
Search for space suit parts.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.130
There's one suit here.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:35.590
That's a mock-up. If you wear it outside,
you will die instantly.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:36.930
A wheelchair.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:38.930
What's this?

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.350
This is an air lock.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.020
Found them. Space suits.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.780
We have one children's bubble,

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:55.030
the two atmospheric pressure suits
that Taiyou found

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.240
and an online suit that is off-line.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:00.790
Chief has the Orlan, so we are short two.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.200
Are the ONIQLOs we're wearing now no good?

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.120
This is like a casual life jacket.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.750
You won't even last five minutes out there
in one of these.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.800
What do you mean "won't last"?

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.630
-You will burst.
-Burst?

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:21.890
At this atmospheric pressure,
the nitrogen in your blood is low.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:23.890
Touya, are you saying that--

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:27.140
Yeah. It might be possible
to go outside in an ONIQLO.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.940
But didn't you say
you would burst in an ONIQLO?

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:33.070
That's if you put in air
at one atmosphere of pressure.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.360
Are you talking about decompression?

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.860
What the hell is wrong
with this space suit?

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.370
That's the suit for total beginners.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:43.700
I can't connect to the Internet.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.460
Well, I'm in a bubble for children.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.670
I wanted to do an EVA.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.170
Full systems check.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:55.170
Suit, check. Oxygen, check.
Communications, check.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.590
Closing the hatch.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:00.430
-Airtightness call.
-Airtight, check.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:03.600
Konoha, disengage
the atmospheric-pressure suit lock.

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:08.390
Konoha and Mina will secure Nasa
to a wheelchair.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:10.900
Closing the decompression room.

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:14.440
We will leave last.

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.690
We will decompress as we walk,

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.950
but we don't have enough time
to fully decompress.

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:23.580
We will get decompression sickness,
but we won't die.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:27.250
You will feel intense pain and nausea,

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:30.290
but you have to tolerate it
until you get to the other side.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.670
Okay, here we go!

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.640
Listen to me, Earthers.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:43.550
We off-Earthers have a duty

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:48.230
to protect and preserve untrained Earthers
in times like these.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.860
No matter what, we will keep you alive
and return you to Earth.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:56.230
Walk to that Mars dome.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:02.070
Chief,
don't let Hakase roll off the pathway.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.120
Everyone, follow behind the chief.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.540
My suit is inflating. I can't walk.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.580
Let the air out of your suit.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.800
Doesn't the Earth look a little closer
than it did before?

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:30.060
Why is there snow over there?

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.940
What is that pattern?

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:34.310
It's an "S" Pattern.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:36.820
Nasa, are you all right?

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:41.650
It is a sacred formula that appears
over and over in the Seven Poem.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:43.240
The "S" Pattern?

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.950
Comet?

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:53.000
-Konoha, what's the matter?
-Konoha, keep walking!

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.750
A comet.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:58.500
A comet is coming.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:04.470
-Why is a comet heading this way?
-And at such a time!

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:09.180
-Where am I?
-Chief, you back with us?

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.140
Yes. What's the situation now?

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:13.980
There's comet debris coming this way.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:16.480
It seems the time has come to use it.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:20.230
Body-expanse operation!

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:23.360
How macho!

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.830
-The comet!
-Run!

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:58.810
Taiyou!

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:12.240
Taiyou!

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.430
Oh, no.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:34.730
Just a little farther. Reach for--

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:46.490
Remove the tether.

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.950
Damn it, I can't.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:53.330
I can't hold on any longer.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:57.000
It's pulling me!

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:10.180
Not bad for an Earther.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:11.260
You too.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:16.770
Touya,
an hour ago you said Earthers should die.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.150
Shut up, Earther.

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:31.030
I treated you guys like idiots
because you are Earthers,

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.660
but you're not so bad.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:35.950
I'm honored!

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.540
You don't have to force yourself
to say leader-like things.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:42.630
Detachment function not in operation.
Detachment--

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:45.050
I'm never wearing this space suit again!

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:49.430
If we climb up here, we should be able
to get to the control room.

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:51.760
What is this grater-like thing?

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:53.640
The heavy bulkhead is closed.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.310
Can't we open it manually?

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:58.600
We can't open heavy bulkheads
without Twelve.

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.440
Another dead end?

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.480
The wall's wireless charger is working.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:08.070
The electrical network
is starting to self-repair.

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:12.030
If I can bypass this,
I can probably restore it.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.450
Electricity!

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:23.210
This is the Mars Development
Historical Museum.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.670
Ready, go.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:33.300
Incidentally,
isn't this surface a little unusual?

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:34.930
You're right.

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:37.100
The ground is turning.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:38.890
I see.

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:42.690
Look,
it's because the rotations make gravity.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:44.940
The ground is turning on this circle.

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.400
See?

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:50.030
The gravity on this side is tilted.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.950
I do wired recharging.

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:53.030
PATHWAY TO C CYLINDER CLOSED

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:54.950
There's a breach in this pathway too?

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:57.080
So this is another dead end.

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:59.620
How long will this fabric bulkhead last?

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:01.080
About half a day, I think.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.540
Can we use the convenience store?

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:04.920
My treat.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.000
GENUINE PRODUCTS

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:08.420
Gather the necessary supplies
and eat what you want.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:12.090
-Mighty Anshin-kun!
-With pleasure.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:16.010
Thank goodness. It still works.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:25.520
The "S" Pattern.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.190
Nasa mentioned it earlier.

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.870
What? "Comet water."

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:40.080
This is the comet water
picked up on the rocket, isn't it?

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:41.790
It's not from the rocket.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:45.000
The comet itself is melted down,
turned into plasma and injected.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.920
Ah, plasma. Yes. I know.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.670
Plasma is tasty, isn't it?

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:52.090
Damn it.

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:54.090
Can't see it from here either.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.680
What's the matter, Touya?

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:59.560
I want to check
if the control room is secure.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:02.220
Yeah, can't see it from here.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:06.150
If only we had an Internet connection,

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:08.690
I would be able to see it
with my cyber glasses.

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:10.400
OUT OF RANGE

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:11.650
Uncle.

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:16.360
We'll definitely be able to see it
from another window. I'll go look.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.120
UNCLE, STILL ALIVE? REPLY.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:21.370
MESSAGE FAILED TO SEND

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:23.910
It's supposed to be right above.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:25.620
Touya.

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.380
Thanks for before.

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:34.630
Yeah, you too.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:40.800
This comet water was also harvested
by Seven Technology, wasn't it?

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.260
That's right.

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:44.930
Even so, it's just normal water, isn't it?

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.140
Yeah.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:51.860
I bet you hate Seven, don't you?

00:17:55.150 --> 00:18:01.240
Lunatic is probably behind Seven's
design flaws in your implants.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:06.460
I still don't know a lot about Lunatic.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.250
The Seven on the moon's surface

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:12.290
back then dramatically advanced
their intelligence without reason.

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:14.210
They lost control,

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:17.300
and eventually the "Frame" intelligence
framework was destroyed on its own,

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:18.800
and the intelligence collapsed.

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:23.850
They also lost control of the products
designed by Seven in a chain reaction,

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:26.230
and many accidents
occurred around the globe.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:29.650
We found out that
the number of casualties from this event

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.690
was in the thousands.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:38.240
UN2 made cognitive limiters compulsory
in order to prevent another Lunatic,

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:41.160
so that a disaster like that
never happens again.

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:46.160
As your friend, I want to help you.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.620
Hand over that drone.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.000
Please let me do the right thing.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:55.960
You don't have to wake up Lunatic.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:19:00.050
If my dad uses his connections at UN2,
we can find a solution for your implant.

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.470
No.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.220
Why not?

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:07.310
You couldn't possibly want
to cause another event like Seven.

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:08.850
You don't understand anything.

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:12.150
Don't you hate Seven?

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:14.730
If Seven had used cognitive limiters,

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:17.440
you never would have had
to suffer like this.

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:19.110
Yeah.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:21.740
If we didn't have the Seven implants,

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:24.950
we would have died
when we were even younger.

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:28.040
I told you before.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.910
The implants worked when we were little.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.460
If limiters were put on by Seven,

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:36.670
we would have died at three
like the other ten did.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:37.920
But--

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:40.050
Seven didn't fail.

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:43.010
It just found a method
that didn't work well.

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:45.640
But will you sacrifice yourself for that?

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:48.680
-You'll die.
-I'm not dead yet.

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:50.480
What about Konoha?

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:54.810
If Seven hadn't been euthanized,
its intelligence would have expanded

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:58.030
and it eventually would have found
a method that succeeded.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:00.490
It's UN2 that failed.

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:06.240
I'm going to destroy
all of the UN2's cognitive limiters,

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:09.410
complete an AI that surpasses Seven

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:11.120
and live.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.120
I'm not going to die.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:14.790
Neither will Konoha.

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:20.300
I'm not done talking!

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.300
The pain is back.

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:24.890
Nasa.

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:27.300
There's a Smart printer
at the convenience store.

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:30.810
We're having a print-spree.
Isn't this great?

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:34.560
Your Smart is the old seal-style one,
isn't it?

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:36.190
Get this one.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:39.110
Well, I'm happy with this one.

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:41.690
Is that a printer too?

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:44.570
Yes. I thought I could make a brace.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:46.490
Are you okay? Does it hurt?

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:49.620
I'm fine. It doesn't hurt anymore.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:51.080
Oops!

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:58.290
Nasa, thank you for protecting us.

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:00.630
Thank you.

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:02.300
Oh, no.

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:05.930
I mean, it's my job
to ensure the safety of our guests.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.470
How is your injury?

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:09.890
I'm totally fine now.

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:13.140
I'm in charge
of this station's health care after all.

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:16.600
See? Now quit bothering me
and go play over there.

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:18.650
I hate kids, you know.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.150
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:22.860
I'm tired.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:26.740
I really can't stand kids.
Yet kids love me.

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:29.410
Ouch.

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.240
We must hurry.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:38.750
-The sun set.
-It's night mode.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:43.760
The Seven that surpassed
human intelligence and fell to Lunatic

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:47.720
kept spitting out cryptic formulas
that didn't make sense

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:50.140
and caused numerous accidents.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:53.520
That's the Seven Poem, right?
It was in the Monthly Mar magazine.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:54.600
THE TRUTH OF LUNATIC SEVEN

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:57.690
False rumors started spreading that it was
an encrypted prophecy of the future,

00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:02.020
and the UN2 as well as some
research institutions tried to solve it.

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:03.730
But there was no correct answer.

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:06.280
It was only used as an excuse
for occultists to make money

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:09.780
and by groups like John Doe
to carry out terrorist acts.

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:14.700
But there is still information
that has not been publicized.

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:17.750
Somebody actually deciphered
a small portion of it.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:21.130
This is what it said.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:27.420
36.79% of humanity
needed to be euthanized right away.

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:31.430
That's true, isn't it?

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:35.810
My father wanted to go public with it,

00:22:35.890 --> 00:22:38.560
and he lost his position at the UN2.

00:22:39.140 --> 00:22:42.150
In order to restore my father's name,

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:44.650
I want to tell the world
the truth about Lunatic

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:47.320
and restore the UN2 to its original form.

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:50.200
Do you know the truth?

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:54.620
Before Lunatic, Seven said this,

00:22:55.290 --> 00:22:57.870
that humanity must leave its cradle

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:01.210
and have and raise children off of Earth.

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:04.750
Back then, ten children died on the moon,

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:08.920
and then most humans ended up
opposing space exploration.

00:23:10.010 --> 00:23:12.800
They said humans needed
to return to Earth.

00:23:13.510 --> 00:23:15.970
But where are we supposed to go home to?

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:19.430
Those of us who cannot
withstand Earth's gravity

00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:22.560
have no home to return to.

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:28.240
Seven was our only ally.

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:30.780
Seven's words alone

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:34.370
have supported me and Konoha
this entire time.

00:23:35.700 --> 00:23:38.080
I guess what I said is useless.

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:41.160
Let's talk later.

00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:46.920
It's a little different
from the Seven Poem again.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:49.920
Yes, it's rushing into a new branch.

00:23:51.050 --> 00:23:52.260
Konoha.

00:23:52.340 --> 00:23:54.590
I brought a first aid kit.

00:23:55.510 --> 00:23:57.010
Oh, thanks.

00:23:57.100 --> 00:23:58.560
Ouch.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:01.770
Is there an auto-diagnosis patch?
It looks like a compress.

00:24:02.730 --> 00:24:04.520
-This?
-Yeah.

00:24:04.600 --> 00:24:06.110
Oh, it hurts.

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:08.230
Nasa, am I--

00:24:09.990 --> 00:24:11.740
Am I going to die soon?

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:14.780
What's brought this on all of a sudden?

00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:19.870
I've been light-headed lately,
and it's getting worse.

00:24:19.950 --> 00:24:22.000
Don't be silly.

00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:24.500
I'm the one who looks more likely to die.

00:24:26.250 --> 00:24:27.880
Why do you say that?

00:24:29.090 --> 00:24:32.760
You know a lot about Seven, don't you?

00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:38.010
I wonder how Seven felt.

00:24:39.760 --> 00:24:41.600
Right before Seven died,

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:44.770
it was the smartest it had ever been.

00:24:45.560 --> 00:24:47.980
It was also able
to see everything in the future,

00:24:48.060 --> 00:24:50.190
so it left the Seven Poem.

00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:55.610
That means it knew it was going to die,
didn't it?

00:24:58.490 --> 00:25:02.330
It saw its own death,
the end of the world. It saw everything.

00:25:02.410 --> 00:25:06.460
Even so, it continued to look
into the future for humanity's sake.

00:25:08.170 --> 00:25:12.550
I feel like I kind of understand
how Seven felt.

00:25:12.630 --> 00:25:13.880
Konoha.

00:25:14.510 --> 00:25:19.550
Surely it saw through everything--
as if it were clear, clean water--

00:25:21.140 --> 00:25:24.020
and it died with no regrets.

00:25:25.310 --> 00:25:27.940
When I think about that, I--

00:25:29.520 --> 00:25:32.030
I'm no longer afraid of dying.

00:25:36.450 --> 00:25:39.160
It let me live 14 years.

00:25:40.700 --> 00:25:44.790
If Seven says I am going to die soon,

00:25:45.620 --> 00:25:47.830
-I have peace of mind--
-Konoha.

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:51.170
We will all die.

00:25:51.250 --> 00:25:53.130
That's a fact.

00:25:53.210 --> 00:25:55.050
But not now.

00:25:55.760 --> 00:25:59.220
Also, the future will end soon.

00:25:59.300 --> 00:26:00.300
What?

00:26:00.390 --> 00:26:02.220
The fixed future, that is.

00:26:02.850 --> 00:26:05.770
The Seven Poem is the story of the end.

00:26:07.060 --> 00:26:10.230
Oh, yeah. I'll tell you a special secret.

00:26:12.520 --> 00:26:13.690
FiTsZ.

00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:16.740
FiTsZ.

00:26:16.820 --> 00:26:18.610
It's a secret word.

00:26:18.700 --> 00:26:20.030
Memorize it.

00:26:22.080 --> 00:26:26.120
My cyber glasses can connect
to the Internet and peer comms.

00:26:26.200 --> 00:26:27.120
SPACE DRONE PHOTOS

00:26:27.210 --> 00:26:28.870
A sightseeing drone.

00:26:31.750 --> 00:26:33.750
Touya!

00:26:35.420 --> 00:26:36.970
I figured it out.

00:26:37.050 --> 00:26:41.180
We can connect the photo drone
for tourists to peer-to-peer.

00:26:42.510 --> 00:26:43.930
We have a way to do that?

00:26:45.720 --> 00:26:47.020
It connected.

00:26:51.440 --> 00:26:53.150
The video has come through.

00:26:54.400 --> 00:26:56.860
That's the crab that pinched me earlier.

00:26:58.860 --> 00:27:01.740
The shuttle. There's no shuttle.

00:27:01.820 --> 00:27:04.080
The entire shuttle area is gone.

00:27:04.160 --> 00:27:06.830
-The shuttle!
-I can see it!

00:27:11.170 --> 00:27:13.790
What a relief. The control room is safe.

00:27:17.010 --> 00:27:18.470
No way.

00:27:18.550 --> 00:27:22.050
No one will die on this station today.

00:27:22.140 --> 00:27:23.350
Nobody.

00:27:23.850 --> 00:27:25.100
Uncle.

00:27:25.180 --> 00:27:28.390
Touya, don't give up yet. Think.

00:27:29.140 --> 00:27:32.100
When the control room
is no longer usable--

00:27:32.190 --> 00:27:35.400
-Touya, the sub-control room.
-That's right.

00:27:40.280 --> 00:27:41.650
There's light.

00:27:42.320 --> 00:27:43.570
People.

00:27:44.450 --> 00:27:45.740
Uncle!

00:27:46.740 --> 00:27:48.410
Sagami.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:53.290
We're in a vacuum,
so we can't talk with them like this.

00:27:54.830 --> 00:27:56.670
It's a laser transmission.

00:28:00.010 --> 00:28:02.930
-Touya, are you safe?
-Uncle!

00:28:03.010 --> 00:28:04.140
It's Nasa.

00:28:04.220 --> 00:28:07.850
I am with the three Earthers,
Konoha and the chief.

00:28:08.430 --> 00:28:10.850
Great. That means everyone has survived.

00:28:10.930 --> 00:28:13.770
You've done a great job. Where are you?

00:28:14.350 --> 00:28:16.690
In the B Cylinder, Mars Floor.

00:28:17.190 --> 00:28:21.190
Touya, you have to survive long enough
for the UN2 rescue ship to come.

00:28:21.280 --> 00:28:22.610
We will.

00:28:24.360 --> 00:28:25.740
The night is over.

00:28:26.240 --> 00:28:28.120
Just a little longer, guys.

00:28:28.700 --> 00:28:30.660
We're going to solve the problem.

00:29:55.830 --> 00:29:59.250
Subtitle translation by:
Noelle Marie Hollister
